Backport of the webrtc-dtls 0.12 named-curve selection into 0.10.0.

Without this, the DTLS server flight adopts the peer's most-preferred group
without checking whether it is supported. Current Chromium leads with a
post-quantum hybrid, so the handshake aborts with a fatal IllegalParameter and
ErrInvalidNamedCurve, and the data channel never opens.

Apply with [patch.crates-io] against a vendored copy of webrtc-dtls 0.10.0.

--- a/src/flight/flight0.rs
+++ b/src/flight/flight0.rs
@@
+use crate::curve::named_curve::NamedCurve;
+
@@
-                        state.named_curve = e.elliptic_curves[0];
+                        // Pick the first MUTUALLY supported curve. Taking [0]
+                        // blindly adopts the peer's most-preferred group, which
+                        // for current browsers is a post-quantum hybrid this
+                        // version cannot generate keys for.
+                        for curve in e.elliptic_curves.iter() {
+                            if curve != &NamedCurve::Unsupported {
+                                state.named_curve = *curve;
+                                break;
+                            }
+                        }
